## 2. Two-Stage Preflight Protocol (`M1`, `M4`, `M8`, `M9`)

### Stage A — Read-Only Check at Task Start (Before Gate 1)

1. Inspect repository state without modifying branches or files:
   ```sh
   git fetch origin --prune
   git status --short --branch
   git branch -a --list "*{{ticket_prefix}}*"
   git branch -r --list "origin/release/*"
   git describe --tags --abbrev=0 origin/{{production_branch}}
   ```
2. **Pre-existing uncommitted changes (`M4`)**: If the working tree has modifications outside `.superpowers/work-items/`, stop and ask the user whether to commit them on the current branch, stash them, or abort. Never discard or overwrite them.
3. **Pre-Gate 1 writing boundary (`M1`)**: Until Gate 1 (`requirements.md`) is approved by the user, write only uncommitted work-item documents under `{{work_items_path}}`.

### Stage B — Branch Creation & Baseline Re-Verification (Right After Gate 1)

| Job Type | Ask User First | Base Ref | Parent-Ticket Branch Name (`G2`) | Merge Target(s) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{{preflight_rows}}

1. **Create or switch to the Parent-Ticket branch**:
   ```sh
   git switch -c <branch-name> origin/<base-ref>
   ```
2. **Verify ancestry & freshness when reusing an existing branch**:
   ```sh
   git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<base-ref> HEAD
   git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/<base-ref>
   ```
3. **Re-check baseline facts (`M9`)**: When `origin/<base-ref>` differs from the ref on which `codebase-notes.md` was scanned, run `git diff --stat <scanned-sha> origin/<base-ref> -- <cited-paths>` and update any changed baseline facts.
4. **Record `D-NN` in `codebase-notes.md` (`M8`)**:
   ```text
   D-NN Branch: {{example_branch}}
        Parent Ticket: {{example_parent_ticket}}
        Base: origin/{{example_base}} @ <sha>
        Spec scanned on: <ref> @ <sha> (re-checked, <n> cited paths changed)
        Merge targets: {{example_targets}}
        Work-item docs tracked in Git: {{work_items_committed}}
   ```

See [`references/02-naming-commits-and-merge-strategy.md`]({{ref_02}}) for parent-ticket branch naming, sub-ticket/phase commit checkpoints, and merge rules, and [`references/03-versioning-release-and-gates.md`]({{ref_03}}) for SemVer and release gates.
